README.md:This project builds in the voxl-cross docker image (>= V1.7)
README.md:Follow the instructions here to build and install the voxl-cross docker image:
README.md:https://gitlab.com/voxl-public/voxl-docker
README.md:1) Launch the voxl-cross docker.
README.md:~/git/voxl-tflite-server# voxl-docker -i voxl-cross
README.md:bash-4.3$ ls
README.md:2) Install dependencies inside the docker. You must specify both the hardware platform and binary repo section to pull from. CI will use the `dev` binary repo for `dev` branch jobs, otherwise it will select the correct target SDK-release based on tags. When building yourself, you must decide what your intended target is, usually `dev` or `staging`
README.md:voxl-cross:~$ ./install_build_deps.sh qrb5165 dev
README.md:3) Build scripts should take the hardware platform as an argument: `qrb5165` or `apq8096`. CI will pass these arguments to the build script based on the job target. It's recommended your build script also allow a `native` option that uses the native GCC instead of a cross-compiler. This is handy for local building and testing of hard-ware independent code.
README.md:The build script in this template will build for 64-bit using different cross compilers for each hardware platform. See libmodal-pipe for an exmaple of building for both 64 and 32 bit.
README.md:voxl-cross:~$ ./build.sh qrb5165
README.md:voxl-cross:~$ ./build.sh apq8096
README.md:voxl-cross:~$ ./make_package.sh deb
README.md:voxl-cross:~$ ./make_package.sh ipk
README.md:Optionally add the --timestamp argument to append the current data and time to the package version number in the debian package. This is done automatically by the CI package builder for development and nightly builds, however you can use it yourself if you like.
